 "text": "Hi, how have you been? A sketch is quick and rough, usually only one page, and gives you ideas to explore further. A study is thorough and can be several pages long. Kind of. A sketch is for finding out what you think, a study is for showing someone else. Then think about it like a roadmap. Rough drawings like sketches are perfect for that. People expect them to look rough and rough drawings sell the idea that actual photography will make look pretty. The important details. A sketch is great for showing which hillocks need smoothing out, which river is too wide, and which tree needs to be moved. Sounds like fun. Rough drawings are great for showing which bit of the sky looks like paint dripped on freshly painted walls, and which bit of the mountains looks like sand thrown by wind at low tide.",
